[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: The render reads an export generated from the held graph

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-SCRIBE-EXPORT-PAYLOAD
TITLE: The render reads an export generated from the held graph
DEPTH: implemented
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
A render obtains the export JSON from the held graph rather than by running a
fresh export. StrictDoc's JSON generator is a pure function of a built index --
strictdoc's own server calls it against its live one -- so the daemon runs it
against the resident graph into a directory the caller names, and every
downstream consumer reads the same bytes it reads today.

The payload is written to a directory rather than returned, because the current
export is 10.3 MB. An export reconciles first, like any read.

Nothing downstream changes: wireline, view-check, render and status all consume
the export JSON and none of them imports strictdoc.
<<<
